{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00562",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.91,
      "end_seconds": 13.15,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "Doctor, my chest has gone all tight and I think it's the pollen. I've got hay fever, you see, and I'm frightened it's turned into something worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.88,
      "end_seconds": 23.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "Right, deep breath, you're in the right place. Tell me about the tightness. When did it start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.99,
      "end_seconds": 39.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.45,
      "text": "Sunday. So four days ago. I was watching my nephew at a cricket match, sitting on the grass, and I could feel it creeping in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.85,
      "end_seconds": 47.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "And how would you describe it? A band, a weight, a pinch?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.86,
      "end_seconds": 55.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Like someone's pulled a seat belt tight across the front of me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.65,
      "end_seconds": 64.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Good picture. Is it there all the time, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.36,
      "end_seconds": 73.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "Comes and goes. Worse in the afternoon, and when I'm outside, especially near the park."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.43,
      "end_seconds": 79.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Does anything take the edge off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.6,
      "end_seconds": 90.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.8,
      "text": "Coming indoors and sitting down helps a bit. But then I sit there and worry, which doesn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.97,
      "end_seconds": 96.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "That's very human. Is it actually painful, or just tight?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.28,
      "end_seconds": 102.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "No pain. Just tight. Is that better or worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.26,
      "end_seconds": 114.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Better, as far as I'm concerned. Now, you mentioned hay fever. How long have you had that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.72,
      "end_seconds": 128.68,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "Oh, years and years. It's the same every summer. I'm used to that part, it's this chest thing that's new."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.08,
      "end_seconds": 138.98,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "All right. Let me ask about the rest of you. How are your tummy and bowels?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.67,
      "end_seconds": 145.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Fine. Nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.17,
      "end_seconds": 155.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "Sorry, I keep thinking it's my heart. I lie awake doing the maths on how long I've got."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.53,
      "end_seconds": 172.09,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "I'm glad you said it out loud. Let's check things properly rather than leave you doing sums in the dark. Can I listen to your chest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.88,
      "end_seconds": 179.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Yes, please. Do I need to take my top off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.45,
      "end_seconds": 200.81,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Just lift it at the back. Breathe in and out through your mouth, nice and steady."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.68,
      "end_seconds": 211.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "Your chest is clear all the way down, and your throat looks completely normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.64,
      "end_seconds": 215.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Really? Nothing at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.88,
      "end_seconds": 231.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.99,
      "text": "Nothing worrying on the listening side. I'll clip this little sensor on your finger as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.21,
      "end_seconds": 244.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "Oxygen is 98 per cent and your pulse is 76. Both sit right where I'd want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.88,
      "end_seconds": 249.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "So it's not my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.93,
      "end_seconds": 267.73,
      "duration_seconds": 16.8,
      "text": "I'm not going to put a name on it yet, and I'd rather not guess. Think of your airways as a smoke alarm. Sometimes it's too sensitive and goes off when you've only made toast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.17,
      "end_seconds": 272.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "So the pollen is the toast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.13,
      "end_seconds": 289.34,
      "duration_seconds": 15.21,
      "text": "Possibly, but we can test it instead of assuming. I'd like to arrange a breathing test, spirometry, which you blow into a tube and it measures how well the air moves."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.3,
      "end_seconds": 292.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.66,
      "end_seconds": 303.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "Not at all. It's mostly puffing like you're blowing out birthday candles, as hard as you can, three times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.52,
      "end_seconds": 311.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "I can manage a birthday cake. When would that be?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.2,
      "end_seconds": 328.67,
      "duration_seconds": 15.47,
      "text": "The nurse next door can book it before you leave. I'm not starting any tablets or inhalers today, so you aren't taking anything you don't need."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.5,
      "end_seconds": 336.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "That's a relief, actually. I get nervous about new pills."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.93,
      "end_seconds": 354.83,
      "duration_seconds": 15.9,
      "text": "Understood. Meanwhile, check the pollen forecast in the morning, keep your bedroom window shut on high days, and change your clothes when you come in from outside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.63,
      "end_seconds": 361.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Change my clothes. I never thought of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.26,
      "end_seconds": 371.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "Pollen hitchhikes on your sleeves like a stowaway. Little things like that can make the days easier."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.51,
      "end_seconds": 379.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "I'll try. And I'll try not to google it tonight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.75,
      "end_seconds": 390.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Good plan. Googling at midnight is like asking a stranger for directions in a language you don't speak."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.34,
      "end_seconds": 398.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "Ha. Right. Thank you, doctor, I feel less like I'm drowning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.01,
      "end_seconds": 407.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Good. Off you go, and enjoy the cricket from a deckchair next time."
    }
  ]
}
